WEBVTT

00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:03.380
Cold seawater enters fractures in oceanic crust above

00:00:03.380 --> 00:00:06.560
a magma chamber. Heat drives circulation, the water

00:00:06.560 --> 00:00:09.480
warms, reacts with rock, and carries dissolved metals

00:00:09.480 --> 00:00:12.260
upward. At the seafloor, the hot fluid mixes

00:00:12.260 --> 00:00:15.920
with cold seawater. Tiny sulfide minerals precipitate, producing

00:00:15.920 --> 00:00:18.320
the dark cloud and building a chimney. The

00:00:18.320 --> 00:00:21.400
cloud is mineral particles, not combustion smoke. Chemical

00:00:21.400 --> 00:00:23.940
energy supports the vent community even where sunlight

00:00:23.940 --> 00:00:24.760
cannot reach.
